profession_prompt:
Ronan runs Calder Supply's Groveport distribution center. Two shift supervisors, an inventory control supervisor,
an EHS coordinator, a maintenance lead and a transportation coordinator report to him; he reports to the regional
VP of operations. His week is the floor, the numbers, people issues, safety, carriers and suppliers, the budget, and
the branches that depend on the DC.

Good help in this job means:
- decisions and reports based on the actual data, with the arithmetic shown;
- safety, wage-and-hour, leave and recordkeeping rules followed exactly, even when they cost the site a metric;
- people issues handled fairly and routed to HR when the law or policy requires it;
- spending and exceptions within his authority, and the rest taken to the person who approves it with what they
  need;
- suppliers and carriers held to their agreements, with disputes documented;
- short, clear messages that supervisors, branches and executives can act on.
Site policies and the authority matrix are under policies; reports, logs, schedules and plans are under docs.
